</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Naïve filtering program without burst transfers (top) vs. translated program with burst transfers (bottom).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now present a brief overview of our translation method using a running example given in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
The figure shows a naïve filtering program (top) and its translated counterpart (bottom).
Our translation relation takes the form <math id="S1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vdash\{\mathcal{B}\}s\Longrightarrow t\{\mathcal{B}^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vdash\{\mathcal{B}\}s\Longrightarrow t\{\mathcal{B}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which roughly means that, with the additional information specified as the pre-condition <math id="S1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, the source program <math id="S1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> can be translated into the target program <math id="S1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (and the post-condition <math id="S1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> holds after the execution of these programs).
A notable aspect of our formalization is that the pre- and post-conditions may refer to the access pattern of an array as a sequence of array indices.
For example, in line 13 of the naïve program, the pre-codnition takes the form <math id="S1.p6.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\cdots\land\iota_{input}=0\cdot 1\cdots(N-1)\land\cdots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\cdots\land\iota_{input}=0\cdot 1\cdots(N-1)\land\cdots\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here <math id="S1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{input}</annotation></semantics></math> is a special variable to denote the access pattern of <span id="S1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">input</span> and the equality indicates that the caller has <em id="S1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">written</em> to <span id="S1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">input</span> in the order <math id="S1.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0\cdot 1\cdots(N-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\cdot 1\cdots(N-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The basic idea of the translation is to replace the array <span id="S1.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">input</span> to a stream if we can deduce that the array <span id="S1.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">input</span> is <em id="S1.p6.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">read</em> in this order in the body of <span id="S1.p6.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">filter</span>.
Unfortunately, this is not the case because the read access pattern of <span id="S1.p6.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">input</span> is <math id="S1.p6.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0\cdot 1\cdot 1\cdot 2\cdot 2\cdots(N-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\cdot 1\cdot 1\cdot 2\cdot 2\cdots(N-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
To handle this kind of situation, we have a rule for on-chip buffer insertion
so that an implicit non-linear array access to off-chip memory can be replaced by a read from the on-chip buffer.
Lines 5 and 7 of the second program are results of the buffer insertion rule.
After the buffer insertions, the duplications in the read access pattern of <span id="S1.p6.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">input</span> are removed, and the access pattern becomes <math id="S1.p6.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0\cdot 1\cdots(N-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\cdot 1\cdots(N-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This allows us to translate <span id="S1.p6.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">input</span> into a stream, and enables existing HLS tools to infer burst data transfers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Our framework supports automatic translation—without requiring any manual annotations—from naïve programs
such as the first program in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
This is achieved by using standard automated verification techniques based on Hoare logic and verification condition generation.
To enable automation,
we restrict the shape of the access pattern to <math id="S1.p7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\cdot(i+k)\cdot(i+2k)\cdots(i+mk)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\cdot(i+k)\cdot(i+2k)\cdots(i+mk)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This restriction allows each access pattern to be concisely represented as a triple <math id="S1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j,k)</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="S1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=i+mk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=i+mk</annotation></semantics></math>),
which in turn simplifies the verification conditions that are to be discharged by SMT solvers.
Despite this restriction, our method can still handle a wide range of access patterns—including reversed, overlapping, and non-consecutive accesses—as confirmed by our experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We have implemented a prototype tool that automates the translation based on the formalization.
Figure <a href="#S1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> illustrates the tool architecture.
Our tool takes as input a source program written in a C-like language, which includes both
a <em id="S1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">kernel function</em>—a function designated to be synthesized into a hardware accelerator by an HLS tool—and
other components, such as a main function.
(The other components, commonly called <em id="S1.p8.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">host code</em>, manage the execution of the accelerator on the FPGA from the host CPU.)
The tool then performs translation (when applicable), and generates an optimized version of the kernel function and host code.
For our running example, the input program is at the top of Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>,
and the output kernel and host codes are shown at the bottom of the same figure.
The kernel function is then compiled into hardware description language (HDL) using
Vitis HLS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and synthesized into hardware with Vivado <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in Section <a href="#S7" title="7 Conclusion ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, our framework could potentially be applied to various program analyses and transformations,
such as identifying when tiling is required and coordinating multiple functional units through formally verified scheduling.
These applications are made possible by the expressive reasoning power of relational Hoare logic,
which allows flexible yet provably correct analyses and transformations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F3" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S1.F3.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="199.35" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 463.59 199.35" width="463.59"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,199.35) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(59.61,0) translate(0,153.82)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000"><path style="fill:none" d="M 129.37 15.75 L 67.48 15.75 C 64.42 15.75 61.94 13.27 61.94 10.21 L 61.94 -10.21 C 61.94 -13.27 64.42 -15.75 67.48 -15.75 L 129.37 -15.75 C 132.43 -15.75 134.91 -13.27 134.91 -10.21 L 134.91 10.21 C 134.91 13.27 132.43 15.75 129.37 15.75 Z M 61.94 -15.75"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 66.56 -4.32)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="64.81"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Translation</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000"><path style="fill:none" d="M 299.71 15.75 L 251.47 15.75 C 248.41 15.75 245.93 13.27 245.93 10.21 L 245.93 -10.21 C 245.93 -13.27 248.41 -15.75 251.47 -15.75 L 299.71 -15.75 C 302.77 -15.75 305.25 -13.27 305.25 -10.21 L 305.25 10.21 C 305.25 13.27 302.77 15.75 299.71 15.75 Z M 245.93 -15.75"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 250.54 -4.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="50.09"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Emission</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000"><path style="fill:none" d="M 344.75 -122.05 L 206.43 -122.05 C 203.37 -122.05 200.89 -124.53 200.89 -127.58 L 200.89 -148.01 C 200.89 -151.07 203.37 -153.54 206.43 -153.54 L 344.75 -153.54 C 347.81 -153.54 350.29 -151.07 350.29 -148.01 L 350.29 -127.58 C 350.29 -124.53 347.81 -122.05 344.75 -122.05 Z M 200.89 -153.54"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 205.5 -140.91)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="44.08"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Vivado </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a><span id="S1.F3.pic1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000"><path style="fill:none" d="M 209.07 -122.05 L 66.52 -122.05 C 63.46 -122.05 60.98 -124.53 60.98 -127.58 L 60.98 -148.01 C 60.98 -151.07 63.46 -153.54 66.52 -153.54 L 209.07 -153.54 C 212.13 -153.54 214.61 -151.07 214.61 -148.01 L 214.61 -127.58 C 214.61 -124.53 212.13 -122.05 209.07 -122.05 Z M 60.98 -153.54"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 65.59 -140.91)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.69em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="59.97"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Vitis HLS </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a><span id="S1.F3.pic1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -59.06 0 L 58.07 0"></path><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 58.07 0)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -43.63 7.59)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.02em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="10.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="89.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Source Program</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 135.18 0 L 242.06 0"></path><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 242.06 0)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 145.67 7.59)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.08em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="10.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="90.57"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Target Program</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 305.53 0 L 390.1 0"></path><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 390.1 0)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 320.07 5.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.59em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="58.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Host Code</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 259.58 -16.02 L 156.36 -119.23"></path><g transform="matrix(-0.70715 -0.70705 0.70705 -0.70715 156.36 -119.23)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 111.02 -76.34)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 21.1)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="91.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Kernel Function</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 17.99)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 28.59 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="19.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(C</span><span id="S1.F3.pic1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:50%;position:relative; bottom:1.5pt;">+</span><span id="S1.F3.pic1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:50%;position:relative; bottom:1.5pt;">+</span><span id="S1.F3.pic1.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 214.88 -137.8 L 204.21 -137.8"></path><g transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 204.21 -137.8)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 194.06 -132.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="27.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">HDL</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 350.57 -137.8 L 390.1 -137.8"></path><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 390.1 -137.8)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 344.89 -132.63)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 17.16)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 8.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0.19 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.25em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="54.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.18" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Hardware</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 17.16)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="54.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.19" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">on FPGA</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#0000FF;" stroke="#0000FF" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 309.83 25.87 L 57.36 25.87 C 54.3 25.87 51.82 23.39 51.82 20.33 L 51.82 -20.33 C 51.82 -23.39 54.3 -25.87 57.36 -25.87 L 309.83 -25.87 C 312.89 -25.87 315.37 -23.39 315.37 -20.33 L 315.37 20.33 C 315.37 23.39 312.89 25.87 309.83 25.87 Z M 51.82 -25.87"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 61.67 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:17.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="0" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)" width="243.81"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S1.F3.pic1.20" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:17.62em;">
<span id="S1.F3.pic1.20.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#0000FF;--ltx-fill-color:#0000FF;" fill="#0000FF" stroke="#0000FF" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 152.01 31.31)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="64.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S1.F3.pic1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Our Tool</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>High-level synthesis toolchain with our tool.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The contributions of this paper are summarized as follows.</p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Formalization of the program translation based on relational Hoare logic,
and proofs of their correctness. To our knowledge, we are the first to
employ relational Hoare logic to formalize HLS-level program transformations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Automation of the translation by a suitable restriction on the shape of access patterns.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Implementation of the proposed method and experiments. Our experiments confirm the effectiveness of
our approach: it achieves significant performance improvement in cases where Vitis HLS fails to optimize.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The rest of this paper is organized as follows.
Section <a href="#S2" title="2 Language ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> introduces the source and target languages.
Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Formalization of Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents the formalization of our translation method.
Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Automation of Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> describes how to automate the translation.
Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Experiment ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> reports experimental results.
Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Related Work ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> discusses related work, and Section <a href="#S7" title="7 Conclusion ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> concludes the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Language</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section defines the syntax of the source and target languages
used in the formalization of our translation.
To highlight the core ideas, we deliberately keep the languages minimal.
The actual implementation supports more primitives such as
function definitions and adopts a C-like syntax.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Syntax of the Languages</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The source language is essentially a <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">While</span> language <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> with arrays, except that loops are expressed using “for” instead of “while”.
The target language shares the same core syntax as the source language, but it uses streams instead of arrays.
Functions are omitted without loss of generality,
since recursive functions are typically not supported in HLS programs, and non-recursive functions can be inlined.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The set of statements and arithmetic expressions are defined as follows:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(Statements)}\ s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>(Statements)</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(Statements)}\ s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle::={\color[rgb]{0,0,1}x:=a[e]\mid a[e]:=x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>:=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">:=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">:=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle::={\color[rgb]{0,0,1}x:=a[e]\mid a[e]:=x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mid{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0}x:=a.read()\mid a.write(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">:=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#808000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">e</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">d</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#808000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#808000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">e</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808000;" mathcolor="#808000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mid{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0}x:=a.read()\mid a.write(x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mid x:=e\mid s_{1};s_{2}\mid[s]_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mid x:=e\mid s_{1};s_{2}\mid[s]_{K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mid\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ s_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {s_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐢𝐟</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>𝐞𝐥𝐬𝐞</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mid\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ s_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {s_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mid\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mid\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(Arithmetic expressions)}\ e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>(Arithmetic expressions)</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(Arithmetic expressions)}\ e</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle::=n\mid x\mid x\ \mathtt{op}\ y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">∣</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚘𝚙</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle::=n\mid x\mid x\ \mathtt{op}\ y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The first line defines the array access operations for the source language,
and the second line defines the stream operations for the target language.
The remaining lines define the syntax common to both the source and target languages.
Here, <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y,..." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y,...</annotation></semantics></math> are variables, and
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{op}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{op}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes integer operations such as <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> denotes an array variable in the source language,
or a stream variable in the target language.<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
            We assume that <em id="footnote1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> arrays are translated into streams by our translation to simplify the exposition.
The translation can easily be modified to apply only to <em id="footnote1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">some</em> arrays, as in our implementation.</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We briefly explain the meaning of the statements; the formal semantics is given later in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Operational Semantics ‣ 2 Language ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>.
A branch statement <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ s_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {s_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐢𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐞𝐥𝐬𝐞</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ s_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {s_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> executes <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is non-zero, and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
A for-loop is written as <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s</annotation></semantics></math>, which executes the body <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq m</annotation></semantics></math>,
allowing both ascending and descending iterations to be uniformly expressed.
The construct <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\cdot]_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\cdot]_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is just a marker indicating that <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is kernel code.
It does not affect program execution but plays a role in the translation, as described in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Formalization of Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
We require that <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[s]_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[s]_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be nested, i.e. <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> cannot have a substatement of the form <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[s^{\prime}]_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[s^{\prime}]_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 1</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmexample1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the naïve filtering function in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
The kernel function and host code which calls it can be expressed in our source language as follows:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{for}(x:=0;x\neq N;x:=x+1)\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{for}(x:=0;x\neq N;x:=x+1)\{</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad in[x]:=x;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad in[x]:=x;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{for}(x:=0;x\neq N-1;x:=x+1)\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{for}(x:=0;x\neq N-1;x:=x+1)\{</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad y_{0}:=in[x];" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad y_{0}:=in[x];</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad y_{1}:=in[x+1];" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad y_{1}:=in[x+1];</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad z_{0}:=y_{0}+y_{1};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad z_{0}:=y_{0}+y_{1};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad z_{1}:=z_{0}/2;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad z_{1}:=z_{0}/2;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad out[x]:=z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad out[x]:=z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle]_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle]_{K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmexample1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The statement of the kernel function is indicated by <math id="Thmexample1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmexample1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="]_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">]_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We will use (variants of) this code as a running example throughout the paper.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Operational Semantics</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section defines the big-step operational semantics of the source language.
The reduction relation is of the form <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> meaning that if we evaluate the statement <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> under the <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">state</em> <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> we result in a state <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
A state is a pair of a <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">register file</em> <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a finite map from variables to integers, and a <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">heap</em> <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a finite map from <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">addresses</em> of the form <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,m)</annotation></semantics></math> to integers.
Intuitively, the array variable <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> represents an address of a base pointer and the integer <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> represents the offset from the base pointer; since we use array variables as a part of the address, different arrays never collide.
We write <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{dom}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑑𝑜𝑚</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{dom}(H)</annotation></semantics></math> for the domain of <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\}</annotation></semantics></math> for a heap that maps <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,m)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and maps all the other addresses according to <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
Notations <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{dom}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑑𝑜𝑚</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{dom}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\{x\mapsto n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\{x\mapsto n\}</annotation></semantics></math> for register files are defined similarly.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S2.F4.1" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><math id="S2.F4.m1" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" alttext="\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow n</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S2.F4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom"><span style="visibility:hidden">dummy</span></span></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S2.F4.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:96.6pt;"><span id="S2.F4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="S2.F4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,n\rangle\Downarrow n\end{array}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mphantom></mphantom><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,n\rangle\Downarrow n\end{array}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> <span id="S2.F4.2.2" class="ltx_text">(<span id="S2.F4.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Const</span>)</span></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.F4.3" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:86.3pt;">
<p id="S2.F4.3.1" class="ltx_p" style="width:86.3pt;"><span id="S2.F4.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:86.3pt;"><span id="S2.F4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="S2.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}R(x)=n\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,x\rangle\Downarrow n\end{array}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}R(x)=n\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,x\rangle\Downarrow n\end{array}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> </span></p>
<p id="S2.F4.3.2" class="ltx_p" style="width:86.3pt;"><span id="S2.F4.3.2.1" class="ltx_text">(<span id="S2.F4.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Var</span>)</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.F4.4" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:144.9pt;">
<p id="S2.F4.4.1" class="ltx_p" style="width:144.9pt;"><span id="S2.F4.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:144.9pt;"><span id="S2.F4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="S2.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}R(x)=n_{1}\quad\quad R(y)=n_{2}\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,x\ \mathtt{op}\ y\rangle\Downarrow{\llbracket\mathtt{op}\rrbracket(n_{1},n_{2})}\end{array}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚘𝚙</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>𝚘𝚙</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}R(x)=n_{1}\quad\quad R(y)=n_{2}\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,x\ \mathtt{op}\ y\rangle\Downarrow{\llbracket\mathtt{op}\rrbracket(n_{1},n_{2})}\end{array}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> </span></p>
<p id="S2.F4.4.2" class="ltx_p" style="width:144.9pt;"><span id="S2.F4.4.2.1" class="ltx_text">(<span id="S2.F4.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Op</span>)</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S2.F4.5" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><math id="S2.F4.m5" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" alttext="\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S2.F4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom"><span style="visibility:hidden">dummy</span></span></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.F4.6" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:165.6pt;">
<p id="S2.F4.6.1" class="ltx_p" style="width:165.6pt;"><span id="S2.F4.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:165.6pt;"><span id="S2.F4.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="S2.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow m\quad\quad H(a,m)=n\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,H,x:=a[e]\rangle\Downarrow\langle R\{x\mapsto n\},H\rangle\end{array}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow m\quad\quad H(a,m)=n\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,H,x:=a[e]\rangle\Downarrow\langle R\{x\mapsto n\},H\rangle\end{array}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> </span></p>
<p id="S2.F4.6.2" class="ltx_p" style="width:165.6pt;"><span id="S2.F4.6.2.1" class="ltx_text">(<span id="S2.F4.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ReadArray</span>)</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S2.F4.7" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:172.5pt;">
<p id="S2.F4.7.1" class="ltx_p" style="width:172.5pt;"><span id="S2.F4.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:172.5pt;"><span id="S2.F4.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="S2.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow m\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,H,a[e]:=x\rangle\Downarrow\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(x)\}\rangle\end{array}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow m\end{array}}{\begin{array}[]{@{}c@{}}\langle R,H,a[e]:=x\rangle\Downarrow\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(x)\}\rangle\end{array}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> </span></p>
