<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the interpretation <math id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚊</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> do not rely on <math id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> unless they contain <math id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{head}({\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℎ𝑒𝑎𝑑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{head}({\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}})</annotation></semantics></math> as a subterm.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The satisfaction relation <math id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in a standard manner</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\in{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}\in\mathit{setof}(\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mover><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>def</mi></mover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\in{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}\in\mathit{setof}(\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models\mathbf{true}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi>𝐭𝐫𝐮𝐞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models\mathbf{true}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Pt0.A1.Ex126.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">always holds</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}={\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}={\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex127.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>def</mi></mover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\leq{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\leq{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex128.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}\leq\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>def</mi></mover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}\leq\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\in{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\in{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex129.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}\in\mathit{setof}(\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>def</mi></mover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}\in\mathit{setof}(\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\land{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\land{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex130.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\text{ and }R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>def</mi></mover><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\text{ and }R,H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models\neg{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R,H,\Theta\models\neg{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex131.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}R,H,\Theta\not\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>def</mi></mover><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧̸</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{def}}}{{\iff}}R,H,\Theta\not\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{setof}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{setof}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply a cast operator that converts a sequence of indices to a set of sequence.
In the sequel we may simply use the notation <math id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\widetilde{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\widetilde{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, to make the notation concise.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Partiality of the interpretation)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket a\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket a\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as a partial map and we use partial operations such as <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{head}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℎ𝑒𝑎𝑑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{head}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{tail}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑖𝑙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{tail}</annotation></semantics></math> the interpretation of terms may be undefined.
We stipulate that if a formula contains a term whose interpretation is undefined, then its semantics is false.
Another way to deal with this partiality is to define the interpretation of array variables as a total function by using a dummy value, say <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, for the case <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a[e]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a[e]</annotation></semantics></math> is undefined, and add a formula for boundary check such as <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\iota_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\iota_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> for each array access; similarly we can do a “nil check” before taking the head or the tail of a sequence.
While such encoding might be needed when we invoke SMT solvers, here, we do not take this approach to keep the presentation simple.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We list some substitution lemmas that will be used in the sequel.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an integer term and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> be an integer variable.
Suppose that <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we have</span></p>
<ol id="Pt0.A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Pt0.A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket[{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚊</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚊</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket[{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket[{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\rrbracket_{R\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket[{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\rrbracket_{R\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket[{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket[{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R,H,\Theta\models[{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,H,\Theta\models[{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and only if </span><math id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By induction on the structure of terms and formulas.
The case (1), (2) (3) are proved simultaneously, and the proof of (4) uses (1) to (3).
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be an integer term and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> be an array variable.
Suppose that <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we have</span></p>
<ol id="Pt0.A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Pt0.A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket[a\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\mapsto{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\},\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚊</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚊</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket[a\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\mapsto{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{a}}\rrbracket_{R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\},\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket[a\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\mapsto{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{3}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{3}\rrbracket_{R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\},\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket[a\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\mapsto{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{3}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{3}\rrbracket_{R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\},\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket[a\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\mapsto{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\},\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket[a\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\mapsto{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\},\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R,H,\Theta\models[a\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\mapsto{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,H,\Theta\models[a\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{1}\mapsto{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}_{2}\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and only if </span><math id="Pt0.A1.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\},\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto n\},\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I2.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the previous lemma.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="Pt0.A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that </span><math id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(a)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is nonempty. Then we have</span></p>
<ol id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket[(\mathit{tail}(\iota_{a})/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\mathit{tail}(\Theta(a))\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑖𝑙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑖𝑙</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket[(\mathit{tail}(\iota_{a})/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\mathit{tail}(\Theta(a))\}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R,H,\Theta\models[\mathit{tail}(\iota_{a})/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑖𝑙</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,H,\Theta\models[\mathit{tail}(\iota_{a})/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and only if </span><math id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R,H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\mathit{tail}(\Theta(a))\}\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑖𝑙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\mathit{tail}(\Theta(a))\}\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the </span><math id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then we have</span></p>
<ol id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket[\iota_{a}\cdot{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\Theta(a)\cdot n\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket[\iota_{a}\cdot{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\llbracket{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{I}}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\Theta(a)\cdot n\}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R,H,\Theta\models[\iota_{a}\cdot{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">𝚎</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,H,\Theta\models[\iota_{a}\cdot{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathtt{e}}/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and only if </span><math id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R,H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\Theta(a)\cdot n\}\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\Theta(a)\cdot n\}\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By induction on the structure of the index sequence terms and formulas.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.2 </span>Proof of the Correctness</h3>

<section id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h5>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For convenience, the simulation relation <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, will sometimes be written as <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> exhibiting the <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a witness of the simulation relation.
To avoid the overuse of <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\equiv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≡</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\equiv</annotation></semantics></math> for equality of syntactical terms such as integer terms and formulas.
For example, we will write <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\equiv b=a[0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\equiv b=a[0]</annotation></semantics></math>; here the <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\equiv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≡</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\equiv</annotation></semantics></math> represents the syntactical equality whereas <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math> is the equality symbol of the first-order logic.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We start with proving some auxiliary lemmas.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\vdash e:\mathbf{int}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash e:\mathbf{int}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we have <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow n</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},e\rangle\Downarrow n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},e\rangle\Downarrow n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By a straightforward induction on the derivation of the evaluations.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following is a correctness result for the auxiliary relation <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}\bullet\Longrightarrow u\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}\bullet\Longrightarrow u\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
While this is stated as a lemma it may be considered as one of the key parts of the proof of the correctness.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}\bullet\Longrightarrow u\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}\bullet\Longrightarrow u\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then there uniquely exist <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{1},S_{1},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},S_{1},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, and moreover, <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By induction on the derivation of <math id="Thmproofx6.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}\bullet\Longrightarrow u\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}\bullet\Longrightarrow u\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with a case analysis on the last rule used.</p>
<dl id="Pt0.A1.I4" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-InsRBuf</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It must be the case that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\equiv b:={a}.read()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\equiv b:={a}.read()</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{rarray}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{rarray}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐛𝐮𝐟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=[a[\mathit{head}(\iota_{a})]/b,(\mathit{tail}(\iota_{a}))/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ℎ𝑒𝑎𝑑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑖𝑙</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=[a[\mathit{head}(\iota_{a})]/b,(\mathit{tail}(\iota_{a}))/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Observe that the only reduction rule that can be applied to the statement of the form <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b:={a}.read()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b:={a}.read()</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Read</span>.
In order to apply this rule, we must check whether <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}(a)=n\cdot\widetilde{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}(a)=n\cdot\widetilde{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, that is <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is not an empty string.
Indeed, <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-empty because <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>; recall that if <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{head}(\iota_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℎ𝑒𝑎𝑑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{head}(\iota_{a})</annotation></semantics></math> is undefined, then <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> is false.
Therefore, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R_{1},S_{1},b:={a}.read()\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1}\{b\mapsto n\},S_{1}\{a\mapsto\widetilde{m}\}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},S_{1},b:={a}.read()\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1}\{b\mapsto n\},S_{1}\{a\mapsto\widetilde{m}\}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
It remains to show <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta^{\prime}}\langle R_{1}\{b\mapsto n\},S\{a\mapsto\widetilde{m}\}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta^{\prime}}\langle R_{1}\{b\mapsto n\},S\{a\mapsto\widetilde{m}\}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we take <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Theta\{a\mapsto\mathit{tail}(\Theta(a))\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑖𝑙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\{a\mapsto\mathit{tail}(\Theta(a))\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We need to show</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle R(x)=(R_{1}\{b\mapsto n\})(x)\text{ for each $x\mathbin{:}\mathbf{int}\in\Gamma$}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext> for each </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">:</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R(x)=(R_{1}\{b\mapsto n\})(x)\text{ for each $x\mathbin{:}\mathbf{int}\in\Gamma$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathit{Idx}(H,a^{\prime})\supseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta^{\prime}(a^{\prime}))\mbox{ for each $a^{\prime}$ such that $\Gamma(a^{\prime})\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐼𝑑𝑥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> for each </mtext><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext> such that </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathit{Idx}(H,a^{\prime})\supseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta^{\prime}(a^{\prime}))\mbox{ for each $a^{\prime}$ such that $\Gamma(a^{\prime})\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{aligned} &amp;H(a^{\prime},\Theta^{\prime}(a^{\prime})[i])=S{\{a\mapsto\widetilde{m}\}}(a^{\prime})[i]\\
&amp;\quad\mbox{ for each $a^{\prime}$ such that $\Gamma(a^{\prime})\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$, $0\leq i&lt;|\Theta^{\prime}(a^{\prime})|$}\\
&amp;R_{1},H,\Theta^{\prime}\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\end{aligned}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext> for each </mtext><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext> such that </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext>, </mtext><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊧</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{aligned} &amp;H(a^{\prime},\Theta^{\prime}(a^{\prime})[i])=S{\{a\mapsto\widetilde{m}\}}(a^{\prime})[i]\\
&amp;\quad\mbox{ for each $a^{\prime}$ such that $\Gamma(a^{\prime})\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$, $0\leq i&lt;|\Theta^{\prime}(a^{\prime})|$}\\
&amp;R_{1},H,\Theta^{\prime}\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\end{aligned}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Most of these are straightforward consequence of <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
The first condition holds because, only the <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> part of <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has been updated and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> does not have type <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{int}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{int}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The second condition holds because <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{setof}(\Theta^{\prime}(a^{\prime}))\subseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta(a^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{setof}(\Theta^{\prime}(a^{\prime}))\subseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta(a^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}:\mathbf{rarray}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}:\mathbf{rarray}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
The third condition holds since</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(a,\Theta^{\prime}(a)[i])=H(a,\Theta(a)[i+1])=S_{1}(a)[i+1]=S_{1}\{a\mapsto\widetilde{m}\}(a)[i]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(a,\Theta^{\prime}(a)[i])=H(a,\Theta(a)[i+1])=S_{1}(a)[i+1]=S_{1}\{a\mapsto\widetilde{m}\}(a)[i]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i&lt;|\Theta(a)|-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i&lt;|\Theta(a)|-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> for addresses other than <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, the satisfaction relation holds thanks to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 ‣ 0.A.1 Assertion language ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 ‣ 0.A.1 Assertion language ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> with the facts that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket a[\mathit{head}(\iota_{a})]\rrbracket_{R_{1},H,\Theta}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ℎ𝑒𝑎𝑑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket a[\mathit{head}(\iota_{a})]\rrbracket_{R_{1},H,\Theta}=n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix1.p1.m29" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Theta^{\prime}=\Theta\{a\mapsto\mathit{tail}(\Theta(a))\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑖𝑙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{\prime}=\Theta\{a\mapsto\mathit{tail}(\Theta(a))\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-InsWBuf</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u={a}.write(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u={a}.write(b)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{warray}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{warray}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐛𝐮𝐟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=n\not\in\iota_{a}\land a[n]=b\land[(\iota_{a}\cdot n)/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=n\not\in\iota_{a}\land a[n]=b\land[(\iota_{a}\cdot n)/\iota_{a}]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The only reduction rule that can be applied to the statement of the form <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{a}.write(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{a}.write(b)</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Write</span>.
Hence, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R_{1},S_{1},{a}.write(b)\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},S_{1},{a}.write(b)\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and this is the unique resulting state.
We prove that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta^{\prime}}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta^{\prime}}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Theta^{\prime}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{def}}}{{=}}\Theta\{a\mapsto\Theta(a)\cdot n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mover><mo>=</mo><mtext>def</mtext></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{\prime}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{def}}}{{=}}\Theta\{a\mapsto\Theta(a)\cdot n\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> is a chosen witness such that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
It should be noted that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined in the sense that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{\prime}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{\prime}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence without any duplicated element because of the precondition <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\notin\iota_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\notin\iota_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The only nontrivial conditions to check to show that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta^{\prime}}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta^{\prime}}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> are:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathit{Idx}(H,a)\supseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta^{\prime}(a))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐼𝑑𝑥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathit{Idx}(H,a)\supseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta^{\prime}(a))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle H(a,\Theta^{\prime}(a)[\ell])=S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}(a)[\ell]\text{where $\ell=|\Theta^{\prime}|-1$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(a,\Theta^{\prime}(a)[\ell])=S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}(a)[\ell]\text{where $\ell=|\Theta^{\prime}|-1$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle R_{1},H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\Theta(a)\cdot n\}\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊧</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{1},H,\Theta\{a\mapsto\Theta(a)\cdot n\}\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">(The other cases are trivial because the register file is untouched, and the only stream that was modified is that stored in the address <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.)
To check the first condition, since <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{setof}(\Theta^{\prime}(a))=\mathit{setof}(\Theta(a))\cup\{n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{setof}(\Theta^{\prime}(a))=\mathit{setof}(\Theta(a))\cup\{n\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Idx}(H,a)\supseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta(a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐼𝑑𝑥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Idx}(H,a)\supseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta(a))</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to show that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathit{Idx}(H,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐼𝑑𝑥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathit{Idx}(H,a)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This holds because <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H,R_{1},\Theta\models b=a[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H,R_{1},\Theta\models b=a[n]</annotation></semantics></math>.
In more detail, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket a[n]\rrbracket_{H,R_{1},\Theta}=H(a,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket a[n]\rrbracket_{H,R_{1},\Theta}=H(a,n)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket b\rrbracket_{R_{1},H,\Theta}=R_{1}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket b\rrbracket_{R_{1},H,\Theta}=R_{1}(b)</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(a,n)=R_{1}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(a,n)=R_{1}(b)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This equality allows us to prove the second condition because</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(a,\Theta^{\prime}(a)[\ell])=H(a,n)=R_{1}(b)=S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}(a)[\ell]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(a,\Theta^{\prime}(a)[\ell])=H(a,n)=R_{1}(b)=S_{1}\{a\mapsto S_{1}(a)\cdot R_{1}(b)\}(a)[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The satisfaction relation holds by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 ‣ 0.A.1 Assertion language ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-InsMove</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\equiv x:=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\equiv x:=y</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(x)=\mathbf{buf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐛𝐮𝐟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(x)=\mathbf{buf}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(y)\in\{\mathbf{int},\mathbf{buf}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐛𝐮𝐟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(y)\in\{\mathbf{int},\mathbf{buf}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=[y/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=[y/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The rule <span id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Assign</span> is the only rule that can be applied to <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{1},S_{1},x:=y\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},S_{1},x:=y\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus, <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\},S_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\},S_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is the only state such that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R_{1},S_{1},x:=y\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\},S_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},S_{1},x:=y\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\},S_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
We need to check that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\},S_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\},S_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,S\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,S\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, for some <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and the stream pool is unchanged by the reduction, it suffices to check</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle R(z)=R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\}(z)\text{ for each $z:\mathbf{int}\in\Gamma$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext> for each </mtext><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R(z)=R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\}(z)\text{ for each $z:\mathbf{int}\in\Gamma$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{1}\{x\mapsto R_{1}(y)\},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The former holds because <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(z)=R_{1}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(z)=R_{1}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z:\mathbf{int}\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z:\mathbf{int}\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is not of type <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{int}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{int}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The latter is a consequence of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 ‣ 0.A.1 Assertion language ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> together with the facts <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1},H,\Theta\models[y/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1},H,\Theta\models[y/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket y\rrbracket_{R_{1},H,\Theta}=R_{1}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket y\rrbracket_{R_{1},H,\Theta}=R_{1}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-Conseq</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, we have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\}\bullet\Longrightarrow u\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\}\bullet\Longrightarrow u\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\quad\text{and}\quad\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mtext>and</mtext><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\quad\text{and}\quad\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> from the above implication.
Therefore, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}}^{\Theta}\langle R_{1},S_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the induction hypothesis, there uniquely exists <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{1},S_{1},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},S_{1},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}}\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}}\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
It remains to show that <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, but this is obvious from <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}}\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}}\langle R_{2},S_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I4.ix4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊧</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.∎</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we prove the simulation relations for the stream translation.
See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Correctness of translation) ‣ 3.3 Correctness of the Translation ‣ 3 Formalization of Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span><span id="Thmproofx7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Proof of (1))</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By induction on the derivation of <math id="Thmproofx7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> with a case analysis on the last rule used.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the proof, we also do a case analysis on the derivation of the translation.
We assume, without loss of generality, that the derivation of the translation does not contain any use of <span id="Thmproofx7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-InsertL</span>, <span id="Thmproofx7.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-InsertR</span> and <span id="Thmproofx7.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-Conseq</span>.
For <span id="Thmproofx7.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-InsertL</span> and <span id="Thmproofx7.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-InsertR</span>, we can simply apply the Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 ‣ Notation. ‣ 0.A.2 Proof of the Correctness ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
If we have <math id="Thmproofx7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}s\Longrightarrow{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\{u\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}s\Longrightarrow{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\{u\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the last rule used is <span id="Thmproofx7.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-Conseq</span>, then we have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\quad\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\quad\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\}s\Longrightarrow{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\{u\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\}s\Longrightarrow{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\{u\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx7.p2.2" class="ltx_p">So, if <math id="Thmproofx7.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, then from <math id="Thmproofx7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\implies{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is easy to see that we have <math id="Thmproofx7.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}}\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}}\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, if <math id="Thmproofx7.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is shown, then we have <math id="Thmproofx7.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}}\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}}\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, it suffices to prove our claim against <math id="Thmproofx7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\}s\Longrightarrow{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\{u\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}\}s\Longrightarrow{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}_{1}^{\prime}\{u\}</annotation></semantics></math>, implying that we can ignore the use of <span id="Thmproofx7.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-Conseq</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now we proceed to the case analysis.
In what follows, we let <math id="Thmproofx7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> to be the witness of <math id="Thmproofx7.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. we assume that <math id="Thmproofx7.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> has been chosen such that <math id="Thmproofx7.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
We first prove the interesting cases, namely those that involve array accesses and the case for the kernel code.</p>
<dl id="Pt0.A1.I5" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ReadArray</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, we have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R,H,x:=a[e]\rangle\Downarrow\langle R\{x\mapsto n\},H\rangle\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow m\quad\quad H(a,m)=n" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable align="bottom" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">‾</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H,x:=a[e]\rangle\Downarrow\langle R\{x\mapsto n\},H\rangle\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow m\quad\quad H(a,m)=n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By the inversion on the translation rule, we must also have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{b=a[e]\land[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}x:=a[e]\Longrightarrow x:=b\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{b=a[e]\land[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}x:=a[e]\Longrightarrow x:=b\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{rarray}\quad\Gamma(x)=\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma\vdash e:\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐛𝐮𝐟</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{rarray}\quad\Gamma(x)=\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma\vdash e:\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\equiv b=a[e]\land[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\equiv b=a[e]\land[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\equiv x:=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\equiv x:=b</annotation></semantics></math>.
Observe that we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(a,m)=n=R^{\prime}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(a,m)=n=R^{\prime}(b)</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models b=a[e]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models b=a[e]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, as the matching evaluation, we can take</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},x:=b\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto n\},S^{\prime}\rangle\langle R^{\prime},b\rangle\Downarrow n" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable align="bottom" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">‾</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},x:=b\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto n\},S^{\prime}\rangle\langle R^{\prime},b\rangle\Downarrow n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">using <span id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Read</span>.
It remains to show that <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R\{x\mapsto n\},H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto n\},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R\{x\mapsto n\},H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto n\},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are not modified, the only condition we need to check is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex152" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto n\},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">This follows from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 ‣ 0.A.1 Assertion language ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket a[e]\rrbracket_{R^{\prime},H,\Theta}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket a[e]\rrbracket_{R^{\prime},H,\Theta}=n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-WriteArray</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, the last step of the derivation must be of the form:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle R,H,a[e]:=x\rangle\Downarrow\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(x)\}\rangle\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable align="bottom" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">‾</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle R,H,a[e]:=x\rangle\Downarrow\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(x)\}\rangle\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By the inversion on the translation rule, we also have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{e\not\in\iota_{a}\land[x/b,a\{e\mapsto x\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}a[e]:=x\Longrightarrow b:=x\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{e\not\in\iota_{a}\land[x/b,a\{e\mapsto x\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}a[e]:=x\Longrightarrow b:=x\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=e\not\in\iota_{a}\land[x/b,a\{e\mapsto x\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=e\not\in\iota_{a}\land[x/b,a\{e\mapsto x\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex156"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma(x)=\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{warray}\quad\Gamma\vdash e:\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐛𝐮𝐟</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma(x)=\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{warray}\quad\Gamma\vdash e:\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">As the matching transition, we take <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime},b:=x\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}\{b\mapsto R(x)\},H^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime},b:=x\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}\{b\mapsto R(x)\},H^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
We are left to show that <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(x)\}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime}\{b\mapsto R(x)\},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(x)\}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime}\{b\mapsto R(x)\},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, we need to show that</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex157"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(a,\Theta(a)[i])=S^{\prime}(a)[i]\mbox{ for each $a$ such that $\Gamma(a)\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$, $0\leq i&lt;|\Theta(a)|$}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> for each </mtext><mi>a</mi><mtext> such that </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext>, </mtext><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(a,\Theta(a)[i])=S^{\prime}(a)[i]\mbox{ for each $a$ such that $\Gamma(a)\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$, $0\leq i&lt;|\Theta(a)|$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex158"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The other conditions are straightforward consequence of <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is modified only for a buffer variable and the domain of the heap has gotten bigger while <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> remains the same.
To show that the condition on the relation between <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> holds, it suffices to show that <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\notin\Theta(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\notin\Theta(a)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\notin\Theta(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\notin\Theta(a)</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models e\notin\iota_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models e\notin\iota_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket e\rrbracket_{R^{\prime},H,\Theta}=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket e\rrbracket_{R^{\prime},H,\Theta}=m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket\iota_{a}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\Theta(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket\iota_{a}\rrbracket_{R,H,\Theta}=\Theta(a)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The satisfaction relation <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> holds by applying Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 ‣ 0.A.1 Assertion language ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 ‣ 0.A.1 Assertion language ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> to <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix2.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models[x/b,a\{e\mapsto x\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models[x/b,a\{e\mapsto x\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-CallKer</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For this case, we just need to check that <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma^{\sharp}\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma^{\sharp}\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>;the rest of the proof is a straightforward application of the induction hypothesis.
This indeed holds because the two conditions</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex159"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathit{Idx}(H,a)\supseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta(a))\mbox{ for each $a$ such that $\Gamma(a)\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐼𝑑𝑥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑒𝑡𝑜𝑓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> for each </mtext><mi>a</mi><mtext> such that </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathit{Idx}(H,a)\supseteq\mathit{setof}(\Theta(a))\mbox{ for each $a$ such that $\Gamma(a)\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex160"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(a,\Theta(a)[i])=S^{\prime}(a)[i]\mbox{ for each $a$ such that $\Gamma(a)\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$, $0\leq i&lt;|\Theta(a)|$}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> for each </mtext><mi>a</mi><mtext> such that </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext>, </mtext><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(a,\Theta(a)[i])=S^{\prime}(a)[i]\mbox{ for each $a$ such that $\Gamma(a)\in\{\mathbf{rarray},\mathbf{warray}\}$, $0\leq i&lt;|\Theta(a)|$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">of <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> involving the array types are symmetric between <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{rarray}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{rarray}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I5.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{warray}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{warray}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx7.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we prove the remaining cases, which are rather standard.</p>
<dl id="Pt0.A1.I6" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Assign</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the case for <span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ReadArray</span>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Seq</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The last step of the derivation must be of the form:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R,H,s_{1};s_{2}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\langle R,H,s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle\quad\quad\langle R_{2},H_{2},s_{2}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable align="bottom" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">‾</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H,s_{1};s_{2}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\langle R,H,s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle\quad\quad\langle R_{2},H_{2},s_{2}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\equiv s_{1};s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\equiv s_{1};s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By inversion on the translation rule, we must also have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex162"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}s_{1}\Longrightarrow u_{1}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}\quad\text{and}\quad\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}s_{2}\Longrightarrow u_{2}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}\quad\text{with }u\equiv u_{1};u_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\}s_{1}\Longrightarrow u_{1}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}\quad\text{and}\quad\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}s_{2}\Longrightarrow u_{2}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}\quad\text{with }u\equiv u_{1};u_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> from the assumption, we have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex163"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},u_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle\quad\text{and}\quad\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid\mathcal{B}^{\prime\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},u_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle\quad\text{and}\quad\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid\mathcal{B}^{\prime\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by the induction hypothesis.
By applying the induction hypothesis, this time to <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{2},H_{2},s_{2}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{2},H_{2},s_{2}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2},u_{2}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle\quad\text{and}\quad\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid\mathcal{B}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2},u_{2}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle\quad\text{and}\quad\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid\mathcal{B}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-IfTrue</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, we must have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R,H,\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ s_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {s_{2}}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle R(x)=0\quad\quad\langle R,H,s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable align="bottom" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐢𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐞𝐥𝐬𝐞</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">‾</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H,\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ s_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {s_{2}}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle R(x)=0\quad\quad\langle R,H,s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\equiv\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ s_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {s_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>𝐢𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐞𝐥𝐬𝐞</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\equiv\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ s_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {s_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, we must also have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex166"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\land x=0}\}s_{1}\Longrightarrow u_{1}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}\quad\text{and}\quad\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\land x\neq 0}\}s_{2}\Longrightarrow u_{2}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">∧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">∧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">≠</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\land x=0}\}s_{1}\Longrightarrow u_{1}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}\quad\text{and}\quad\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\land x\neq 0}\}s_{2}\Longrightarrow u_{2}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">for <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\equiv\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ u_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {u_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>𝐢𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐞𝐥𝐬𝐞</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\equiv\mathbf{if}\ x\ \mathbf{then}\ u_{1}\ \mathbf{else}\ {u_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 ‣ Notation. ‣ 0.A.2 Proof of the Correctness ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},x\rangle\Downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},x\rangle\Downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus, <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime},H,\Theta\models x=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This together with <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\land x=0}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\land x=0}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, by the induction hypothesis, there exists <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime},u_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},H^{\prime},u_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-IfTrue</span>, we also have <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{1},H_{1},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},H_{1},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as desired.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-IfFalse</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the previous case.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ForExit</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, we have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex167"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle R,H,\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H\rangle\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow k\quad\quad k\geq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable align="bottom" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">‾</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle R,H,\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H\rangle\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow k\quad\quad k\geq m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\equiv\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\equiv\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the inversion on the translation rule, we have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex168"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\Gamma\vdash\{[e/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}s\Longrightarrow\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x\geq m\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∧</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\Gamma\vdash\{[e/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}s\Longrightarrow\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x\geq m\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\equiv\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\equiv\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=[e/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=[e/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow k</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},e\rangle\Downarrow k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},e\rangle\Downarrow k</annotation></semantics></math> by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 ‣ Notation. ‣ 0.A.2 Proof of the Correctness ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
Therefore, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> using <span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ForExit</span>.
We can check that <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x\geq m}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∧</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x\geq m}^{\Theta}\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as in the case of <span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ReadArray</span> and <span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Assign</span>.
The only difference is that, in this case, we additionally need to check <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},H,\Theta\models x\geq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},H,\Theta\models x\geq m</annotation></semantics></math>, but this trivially holds because <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix5.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\}(x)=k\geq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\}(x)=k\geq m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ForLoop</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, the last rule of the derivation is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\begin{multlined}\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow k\quad\quad k&lt;m\quad\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H,s^{\prime}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\\
\\
s^{\prime}\equiv{s_{1};\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}}\end{multlined}}{\langle R,H,\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="1.000em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\begin{multlined}\langle R,e\rangle\Downarrow k\quad\quad k&lt;m\quad\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H,s^{\prime}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\\
\\
s^{\prime}\equiv{s_{1};\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}}\end{multlined}}{\langle R,H,\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\equiv\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\equiv\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Observe that this means that there exists a state <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H,s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H,s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{2},H_{2},\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{2},H_{2},\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the inversion on the translation rule, we have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x&lt;m}\}s_{1}\Longrightarrow u_{1}\{[x+n/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">′′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">∧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x&lt;m}\}s_{1}\Longrightarrow u_{1}\{[x+n/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex170"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u\equiv\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u\equiv\mathbf{for}(x:=e;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex171"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=[e/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime},\text{ and }{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}={\color[rgb]{1,0,1}{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x\geq m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">′′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">∧</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">≥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF">m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}=[e/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime},\text{ and }{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}={\color[rgb]{1,0,1}{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x\geq m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.4" class="ltx_p">It is easy to check that we have <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x&lt;m}\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∧</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x&lt;m}\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.

By applying the induction hypothesis to <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H,s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R\{x\mapsto k\},H,s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain a state <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},S^{\prime},u_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto k\},S^{\prime},u_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{2},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid[x+n/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{2},H_{2}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid[x+n/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{2}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now we apply the induction hypothesis to <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{2},H_{2},\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{2},H_{2},\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
To this end, we first show that</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{[x+n/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{[x+n/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex172.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)s_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex173"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow{\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1}}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow{\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1}}\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.5" class="ltx_p">This is derivable by applying <span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-For</span> to (<a href="#Pt0.A1.E1" title="In item R-ForLoop ‣ Proof (Proof of (1)) ‣ Notation. ‣ 0.A.2 Proof of the Correctness ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
We can now apply the induction hypothesis, and obtain a state <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R_{1}^{\prime},S_{1}^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1}^{\prime},S_{1}^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime}_{2},H^{\prime}_{2},\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟𝐨𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime}_{2},H^{\prime}_{2},\mathbf{for}(x:=x+n;x\neq m;x:=x+n)u_{1}\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x\geq m}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∧</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime\prime}\land x\geq m}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the rule <span id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ForLoop</span>, we also have <math id="Pt0.A1.I6.ix6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as desired.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
<p id="Thmproofx7.p4.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We only sketch the proof for the opposite direction since the proof is essentially the same.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span><span id="Thmproofx8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Proof Sketch of (2))</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By induction on the derivation of <math id="Thmproofx8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},u\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> with a case analysis on the last rule used.
The nontrivial cases are the case when the rules <span id="Thmproofx8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Read</span> or <span id="Thmproofx8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Write</span> are used or a buffer is accessed.
Since the proof for the other cases are identical to those of (1) we omit these cases.
That is, if the last rule used in the derivation are not the above mentioned rules, then we can use the same rule for the source program to obtain a matching transition; proving the relation <math id="Thmproofx8.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R_{1},H_{1}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime}_{1},S^{\prime}_{1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is done as in the proof of (1).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If <span id="Thmproofx8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Read</span> or <span id="Thmproofx8.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Write</span> are the last rule used, then <math id="Thmproofx8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is of the form <math id="Thmproofx8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x:={a}.read()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x:={a}.read()</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Thmproofx8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{a}.write(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{a}.write(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In these cases, the last ruled applied must be (if we ignore the consequence rule) <span id="Thmproofx8.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-InsertL</span> or <span id="Thmproofx8.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-InsertR</span>.
These cases follows from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 ‣ Notation. ‣ 0.A.2 Proof of the Correctness ‣ Appendix 0.A Correctness of the Translation ‣ Relational Hoare Logic for High-Level Synthesis of Hardware Accelerators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The remaining interesting case is the case <span id="Thmproofx8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-Assign</span>.
That is, the case where the last rule applied is of the form:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},x:=e\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto n\},S^{\prime}\rangle\langle R^{\prime},e\rangle\Downarrow n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable align="bottom" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">‾</mo></mover></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime},x:=e\rangle\Downarrow\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto n\},S^{\prime}\rangle\langle R^{\prime},e\rangle\Downarrow n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx8.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By the definition of the translation rules, the only cases where this rule involves a buffer is the when (i) <math id="Thmproofx8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x:\mathbf{buf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐛𝐮𝐟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x:\mathbf{buf}</annotation></semantics></math> or (ii) <math id="Thmproofx8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> is a buffer <math id="Thmproofx8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x:\mathbf{int}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x:\mathbf{int}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We first consider the case (i).
In this case let us rename <math id="Thmproofx8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmproofx8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> so that it is clear that the variable is of type <math id="Thmproofx8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{buf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐛𝐮𝐟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{buf}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By inversion on the transformation rule, we must have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex175"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e\equiv y\quad\Gamma(y)=\mathbf{int}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e\equiv y\quad\Gamma(y)=\mathbf{int}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u\equiv b:=y\quad s\equiv a[e^{\prime}]:=y\quad\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{warray}\quad\Gamma\vdash e^{\prime}:\mathbf{int}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u\equiv b:=y\quad s\equiv a[e^{\prime}]:=y\quad\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{warray}\quad\Gamma\vdash e^{\prime}:\mathbf{int}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\Gamma\vdash\{e^{\prime}\not\in\iota_{a}\land[y/b,a\{e^{\prime}\mapsto y\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}a[e^{\prime}]:=y\Longrightarrow b:=y\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\Gamma\vdash\{e^{\prime}\not\in\iota_{a}\land[y/b,a\{e^{\prime}\mapsto y\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}a[e^{\prime}]:=y\Longrightarrow b:=y\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\equiv e^{\prime}\not\in\iota_{a}\land[y/b,a\{e^{\prime}\mapsto y\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>≡</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\equiv e^{\prime}\not\in\iota_{a}\land[y/b,a\{e^{\prime}\mapsto y\}/a]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx8.p4.2" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="Thmproofx8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx8.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As the matching reduction we can take <math id="Thmproofx8.p4.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(y)\}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(y)\}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmproofx8.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle R,e^{\prime}\rangle\Downarrow m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,e^{\prime}\rangle\Downarrow m</annotation></semantics></math>, using <span id="Thmproofx8.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-WriteArray</span>.
We are left to check that <math id="Thmproofx8.p4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(y)\}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}\{b\mapsto R^{\prime}(y)\},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\{(a,m)\mapsto R(y)\}\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}\{b\mapsto R^{\prime}(y)\},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> under the assumption that <math id="Thmproofx8.p4.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have already showed this in the proof of (1) (the case for <span id="Thmproofx8.p4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-WriteArray</span>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx8.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now we consider the case (ii).
In this case, the last transformation rule applied must be <span id="Thmproofx8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tr-READMem</span>, and thus, we must have</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex179"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u\equiv x:=b\quad s\equiv x:=a[e^{\prime}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u\equiv x:=b\quad s\equiv x:=a[e^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex180"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma(x)=\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{rarray}\quad\Gamma\vdash e^{\prime}:\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐫𝐚𝐲</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐭</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐛𝐮𝐟</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma(x)=\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(a)=\mathbf{rarray}\quad\Gamma\vdash e^{\prime}:\mathbf{int}\quad\Gamma(b)=\mathbf{buf}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex181"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{b=a[e]\land[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}x:=a[e^{\prime}]\Longrightarrow x:=b\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma\vdash\{b=a[e]\land[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}x:=a[e^{\prime}]\Longrightarrow x:=b\{{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A1.Ex182"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\equiv b=a[e]\land[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}\equiv b=a[e]\land[b/x]{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx8.p5.2" class="ltx_p">We can take <math id="Thmproofx8.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R\{R\mapsto H(a,m)\},H\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H,s\rangle\Downarrow\langle R\{R\mapsto H(a,m)\},H\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as the matching transition.
Here, we used the rule <span id="Thmproofx8.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ReadArray</span> and <math id="Thmproofx8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the evaluation result of <math id="Thmproofx8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It remains to show that <math id="Thmproofx8.p5.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R\{x\mapsto H(a,m)\},H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto R^{\prime}(b)\},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R\{x\mapsto H(a,m)\},H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}^{\prime}}\langle R^{\prime}\{x\mapsto R^{\prime}(b)\},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> under the assumption that <math id="Thmproofx8.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF00FF">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle R,H\rangle\sim_{\Gamma\mid{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\mathcal{B}}}\langle R^{\prime},S^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
Again, this is something we already proved in the proof of (1) (the case for <span id="Thmproofx8.p5.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">R-ReadArray</span>).
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
